# .ckir - an authored CKIR program (node graph). A node editor reads this and turns it into CKIR.
# CEIR-31b-1b UI-EFFECT SEPARABLE GAUSSIAN BLUR (the S141 frosted-glass chain blur pass, run H then V x2 iterations).
# sigma = R/3 (R=4, 9 taps) -> the +/-4 window sits at +/-3 sigma (~0.27% truncated). Weights w_i = exp(-i^2/(2 sigma^2))/Sum,
# computed in f64, each ROUNDED TO f32, residual (1 - Sum f32) folded into the CENTER tap so the stored f32 set is symmetric
# and sums (f32, left-to-right) to within 1 ulp of 1.0 (measured 0.99999994; exact 1.0f is unreachable for a symmetric set).
# spec-consts: dir.x@0, dir.y@1 (frame sets (1,0) for the H pass, (0,1) for V); step@2 (frame sets 1/half-res-W for H,
# 1/half-res-H for V -- the default 1/1024 is a PLACEHOLDER, 31b-3 MUST set it per pass). Per tap i in [-4,4]: offset =
# i*step*dir (vec2, NO Vec3 array layer -- the 2D discriminator vs moment_blur), sample uv+offset, weight, accumulate.
# Support: R=4 at half-res ~= 8 full-res texels/pass, x2 iterations. Bootstrapped-via-ckir_write then the builder DELETED;
# the committed file is the source, verified by the reading gate (weights == the sigma=R/3 oracle bit-exact + structure).
schema = 1

